      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "even if you've read the documents, it can be strange.\nI've found I have better results with the calibration if I do a Real-Life T-pose while looking straight forward before pressing both triggers.  I don't know if this is a bug, or a nuance of my trackers, or \"working as intended, suggested by the devs\" but it doesn't appear in the documents from what I've seen.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-26T23:16:25.356Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "There are a lot of people who get full-body for the first time and don't understand how to calibrate, (lining spheres up and pressing both triggers on the controllers) because there's no explanation in-game, you're expected to either read the docs (https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/full-body-tracking#using-full-body-tracking-in-vrchat) or have been explained this process by a friend.\nSomething akin to the message about Safe Mode being on would be good. It would be automatically dismissed when you finish calibration.",
